<mxCell id="lgBL" value="Outbound / private flow" style="text;html=1;fontSize=11;fontFamily=Segoe UI;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="66" y="920" width="160" height="20" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
<mxCell id="steps" value="&lt;b&gt;Inbound&lt;/b&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;① The client calls the function's HTTPS endpoint (Microsoft Entra ID / Easy Auth).&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Outbound&lt;/b&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;1 The function sends all outbound traffic through VNet integration (a virtual interface in the delegated subnet).&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;2 Private DNS resolves orders.internal.contoso.com to the internal load balancer.&lt;br&gt;3 The internal NGINX ingress routes the request to the orders-api Service and pods (synchronous path).&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;4 For asynchronous work, the function enqueues to Service Bus through its private endpoint using its managed identity.&lt;br&gt;5 KEDA reads the queue length and scales the queue-worker pods, which receive the messages (workload identity).&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;6 The CSI driver mounts Key Vault secrets.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;7 Nodes pull images from ACR privately.&lt;br&gt;Dashed line: the Functions host reaches its storage account through private endpoints (blob, queue, table)." style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontSize=11;fontFamily=Segoe UI;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="330" y="870" width="1140" height="110" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
</root>
</mxGraphModel>
</diagram>
</mxfile>
